00:29:24.700 --> 00:29:28.490
So, Hipster Chat
has been growing

00:29:28.490 --> 00:29:31.130
and Frank has his
eye on quality.

00:29:31.130 --> 00:29:32.960
He's hungry for
insight so he uses

00:29:32.960 --> 00:29:36.560
Firebase Analytics to learn
how people use his app.

00:29:36.560 --> 00:29:39.080
He's so hungry for
feedback that he

00:29:39.080 --> 00:29:43.690
added a feature where his
users can fill out a survey.

00:29:43.690 --> 00:29:48.160
He's hungrier still, so he
even has an analytics event

00:29:48.160 --> 00:29:51.420
to track when people
fill out the survey.

00:29:51.420 --> 00:29:54.350
And maybe Frank is just hungry.

00:29:54.350 --> 00:29:58.740
Frank was in his coffee shop
munching when he had an idea.

00:29:58.740 --> 00:30:01.070
He wants to incentivize people
to fill out this survey,

00:30:01.070 --> 00:30:02.450
so he's going to
have a giveaway.

00:30:02.450 --> 00:30:04.610
His favorite treat
of vegan gluten

00:30:04.610 --> 00:30:07.730
free kale muffin to
the next 12 people

00:30:07.730 --> 00:30:09.889
who fill out this survey.

00:30:09.889 --> 00:30:11.930
There's a number of reasons
why Frank has already

00:30:11.930 --> 00:30:15.620
marked the feedback sent
event as a conversion event.

00:30:15.620 --> 00:30:18.530
For one, it lets him
create a user funnel

00:30:18.530 --> 00:30:21.980
so you can see what actions
lead people to actually fill out

00:30:21.980 --> 00:30:23.780
surveys.

00:30:23.780 --> 00:30:26.960
Next, he can use this to
create an audience which

00:30:26.960 --> 00:30:30.530
lets him understand whether the
people who fill out his survey

00:30:30.530 --> 00:30:34.790
are actually representative
of his normal demographic.

00:30:34.790 --> 00:30:38.484
And starting today, Frank can
listen to this conversion event

00:30:38.484 --> 00:30:39.400
with a Cloud Function.

00:30:42.380 --> 00:30:46.290
So let's jump back
to the laptop again.

00:30:46.290 --> 00:30:49.960
So for our last
function, we're going

00:30:49.960 --> 00:30:54.080
to create an analytics
event or analytics function.

00:30:54.080 --> 00:30:56.780
So we're listening to
the analytics service

00:30:56.780 --> 00:30:59.714
and for the conversion
event feedback sent.

00:30:59.714 --> 00:31:01.380
This is not a built
in conversion event.

00:31:01.380 --> 00:31:03.920
This is one that Frank
has created on his own

00:31:03.920 --> 00:31:06.170
and marked as conversion.

00:31:06.170 --> 00:31:08.630
Whenever that event is
logged, this code will run.

00:31:12.340 --> 00:31:18.390
So in this case, the event.data
is the full analytics event.

00:31:18.390 --> 00:31:23.500
Because Frank had used
Firebase Analytics.SetUserID,

00:31:23.500 --> 00:31:26.430
this analytic event has
the actual Firebase user

00:31:26.430 --> 00:31:28.890
ID of the person
who sent feedback.

00:31:28.890 --> 00:31:31.050
This is really
important because now he

00:31:31.050 --> 00:31:33.090
can do things like look
up profile information

00:31:33.090 --> 00:31:37.310
or in this case,
give the user a gift.

00:31:37.310 --> 00:31:41.210
Since Frank only has 12
muffin's to give away,

00:31:41.210 --> 00:31:46.850
we're going to add people to the
muffin club in a transaction.

00:31:46.850 --> 00:31:50.180
Now, first he needs to
check whether or not

00:31:50.180 --> 00:31:52.460
he's already given
away all his muffins

00:31:52.460 --> 00:31:55.130
or if he's already given
this user a muffin.

00:31:55.130 --> 00:32:00.690
So if he's given away 12
muffins or he's already

00:32:00.690 --> 00:32:04.770
given this user a muffin, just
exit the transaction early.

00:32:04.770 --> 00:32:05.550
No harm, no foul.

00:32:08.410 --> 00:32:10.540
Otherwise, we'll
log that we're going

00:32:10.540 --> 00:32:12.280
to try to attempt
to give away him

00:32:12.280 --> 00:32:16.800
often and add this user to the
muffin club in our transaction.

00:32:16.800 --> 00:32:20.650
If it succeeds, we'll get a
result that says committed.

00:32:20.650 --> 00:32:22.690
Otherwise it will
retry and will either

00:32:22.690 --> 00:32:25.270
try to modify again or find
out if the last muffin was

00:32:25.270 --> 00:32:27.970
given away and early exit.

00:32:27.970 --> 00:32:31.735
To figure out which
is which, we're

00:32:31.735 --> 00:32:35.200
just going to have
a debug statement.

00:32:35.200 --> 00:32:37.330
So once again, let's
see it in action.

00:32:40.627 --> 00:32:41.720
So let's get feedback.

00:32:44.780 --> 00:32:45.830
I'm being soft on myself.

00:32:49.690 --> 00:32:51.430
I may not have put
this one in debug mode

00:32:51.430 --> 00:32:53.680
so it might take a little
bit for the conversion event

00:32:53.680 --> 00:32:54.620
to come through.

00:32:54.620 --> 00:32:57.640
Let's watch.

00:32:57.640 --> 00:33:00.070
